---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Work with me — Async Forest"
  description="Three ways to work with me: assurance and due diligence, advisory sprints, and ongoing counsel. All of them produce written judgement."
>
  <section class="intro container container--narrow">
    <h1>Work with me</h1>
    <p>
      Three ways to work with me. All of them produce written judgement: what I
      looked at, what I concluded, and why. Everything is scoped in an itemised
      statement of work before we start, and engagements are contracted with
      Async Forest Ltd.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="engagement container container--narrow" id="assurance" aria-labelledby="assurance-heading">
    <p class="engagement__question mono">“Is it sound?”</p>
    <h2 id="assurance-heading">Assurance &amp; due diligence</h2>
    <p>
      An independent review of a system, codebase, or AI integration.
      Point-in-time and scope-limited: the report speaks to what I examined,
      when. You get prioritised, actionable findings and a clear conclusion,
      in writing. A retest is available once findings have been addressed.
    </p>
    <p>
      For investors — technical due diligence and portfolio reviews — boards,
      universities and institutions, and founders preparing to raise.
    </p>
    <p class="engagement__price mono">from £[PRICE SLOT — assurance]</p>
  </section>

  <section class="engagement container container--narrow" id="sprints" aria-labelledby="sprints-heading">
    <p class="engagement__question mono">“What should we do?”</p>
    <h2 id="sprints-heading">Advisory sprints</h2>
    <p>
      A time-boxed sprint, typically two to four weeks, organised around one
      named decision: GenAI architecture, build-vs-buy, scale readiness, the
      technical narrative before a raise. The deliverable is a decision memo —
      the question, the options, the trade-offs, a recommendation and the
      reasoning.
    </p>
    <p class="engagement__price mono">from £[PRICE SLOT — sprint]</p>
  </section>

  <section class="engagement container container--narrow" id="counsel" aria-labelledby="counsel-heading">
    <p class="engagement__question mono">“Keep us honest.”</p>
    <h2 id="counsel-heading">Ongoing counsel</h2>
    <p>
      For teams putting AI into production: a standing fortnightly session,
      async written answers to hard questions, and a quarterly deep-dive, on
      renewable terms. An independent voice before the board meeting, not
      another status call.
    </p>
    <p class="engagement__price mono">structured engagements from £[PRICE SLOT — counsel]/month</p>
  </section>

  <section class="boundaries container container--narrow" aria-labelledby="boundaries-heading">
    <h2 id="boundaries-heading">How I work</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Engagements are point-in-time and scope-limited; the report speaks to what I examined, when.</li>
      <li>Deliverables are written. Meetings are for decisions, not status.</li>
      <li>Regulatory findings (UK GDPR, Children's Code, Online Safety Act, EU AI Act) are technical observations, not legal advice; where legal interpretation is needed I'll say so.</li>
      <li>I'm not a CREST penetration-testing provider; where a formal pen test is required I refer to accredited partners and can scope and interpret it for you.</li>
      <li>Capped time-and-materials on unfamiliar codebases; fixed scope where the ground is known.</li>
      <li>Engagements are contracted with, and reports issued by, Async Forest Ltd, which carries professional indemnity insurance.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="close container container--narrow">
    <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact/">Tell me about the decision you're facing</a>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .intro {
    padding-block: var(--section-y) var(--space-8);
  }
  .intro p {
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .engagement {
    padding-block: var(--space-8);
  }
  .engagement__inner-rule,
  .engagement__question {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    padding-top: var(--space-8);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-default);
  }
  .engagement__price {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .boundaries {
    padding-block: var(--space-8) var(--space-12);
  }
  .boundaries h2 {
    padding-top: var(--space-8);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-default);
  }
  .boundaries li {
    max-width: 68ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .close {
    padding-block: var(--space-8);
  }
</style>
